##* {{RQ:Scott Peveril of the Peak|volume=I|chapter=I|pages=5–6|pageref=6|passage=[H]e had a dispensation for '''conforming''' in outward observances to the Protestant faith.}}
##* {{RQ:Darwin et al Voyages|passage=[B]y '''conforming''' to the dress and habits of the Gauchos, he has obtained an unbounded popularity in the country.|chapter=4}}
##* {{quote-book|en|title=The Book of Sharks|author={{w|Richard Ellis (biologist)|Richard Ellis}}|year=1983|publisher=Knopf|ISBN=0679722106|passage=In any case, most of these sharks are gray or grayish, and they certainly are typical in that they '''conform''' to everyone's idea of what a shark is supposed to look like.|page=110}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|of things or procedures}} To be as [[require|required]] or [[recommend|recommended]] by a [[specification]], [[regulation]], or [[policy]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1919|author=Hildegard G. Frey|title=The Camp Fire Girls Do Their Bit|chapter=11
|passage=In height and breadth it '''conformed''' to the prescribed measurements laid down by the rules of the contest.}}
#* {{RQ:en:New York Times|date=22 Dec 2006|url=http://www.nytimes.com/2006/12/22/business/22vioxx.html|title=Judge Cuts Amount of Vioxx Award|accessdate=7 June 2011
|passage=A judge in a Texas widow’s lawsuit over the Merck drug Vioxx reduced a $32 million jury award to about $7.75 million on Thursday so that it '''conformed''' to state law. {{...}} But Judge Alex W. Gabert, in a Rio Grande City courtroom, ordered the punitive damage reduced to '''conform''' to a 2003 Texas law that caps punitive damages at twice the amount of economic damages — lost pay — and up to $750,000 on top of noneconomic damages.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20220712052917/https://www.nytimes.com/2006/12/22/business/22vioxx.html}}

